        JMPI cc_UC,[R3]

; ======== CapCom_CC0_Ch0_Drv  (@0xa9240) ========
        ; CAPCOM output-compare channel driver, CHANNEL 0 (CC0/CC0IC, P2.0, accumulator DAT_00fa12->fa0a,
        ; state byte DAT_00f59b, fd5a bits 0x40/0x80). One of a 4-channel near-identical cluster (per
        ; cylinder/output): Ch0=0xa9240(CC0), Ch1=0xa9316(CC1,P2.1,fa14,f59c),
        ; Ch2=0xa93ec(CC2,P2.2,fa16,f59d), Ch3=0xa94bc(CC3,P2.3,fa18,f59e). Each ends in RET -> GENUINE
        ; independent functions (NOT tco_sub-style switch-arms), just unnamed. Named by unambiguous HW
        ; channel. Schedules the next compare event (eoi/T0/T7 timing) and integrates/saturates the
        ; per-channel accumulator.
